;; C++'s read level's divergences for repr/cpp's token check (doc/cpp/CPP-SURVEY.md, "As built: CX2", "As built: CX10
;; (write-ahead)"; bin/repr-cpp pp-check): the classes of test/repr/cpp/pp-check-known.edn (CX10, generated from its :classes,
;; their texts; the kinds chosen at CX10: what the compilers settle against each other or a file outside C++ by design, what
;; the port should close deferred), in test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A case is CORPUS/NAME, its reason "CLASS: the class's
;; text" (bin/reap's reader :c-known with :id-sep "/"); a file listed at :pp and :lex one non-pass (:per-file). The dg check's
;; classes are CX9's, test/cpp/divergences-dg.edn. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :gxx-rejects
  :title "g++ -E rejects the file; the port reads it, as the compilers' preprocessors agree on its tokens"
  :kind :design
  :why "g++ -E rejects the file (a pedantic error, an option or a character set it refuses, a header unit): the port reads it, as the compilers' preprocessors agree on its tokens (CX2)"
  :decided "CX2; the kind CX10's; since CP261 (a) (the user, 2026-11-08) such a file is judged by clang's raw tokens alone (pp-check's clang-tokens), a pass: the class keeps one whose raw tokens are not clang's either"
  :match [#"^known gxx-rejects:"]}
 {:id :modules-ts
  :title "a -fmodules-ts file: g++ -E rewrites the import directives, the port reads them as C++20 says"
  :kind :design
  :why "a -fmodules-ts file: g++ -E looks the imported modules up and rewrites the directives (import \"/abs/path\";), the port reads import <h>; as one header-name token as C++20 says (the lexical check); modules beyond a single TU are CP13's"
  :decided "CX2, CP13; the kind CX10's; since CP261 (a) (the user, 2026-11-08) such a file is judged by clang's raw tokens alone (pp-check's clang-tokens), a pass: the class keeps one whose raw tokens are not clang's either"
  :match [#"^known modules-ts:"]}
 {:id :named-ucn
  :title "C++23's named universal character escape \\N{NAME} in an identifier: clang lexes it, the port does not"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "C++23's named universal character escape \\N{NAME} (N3366) in an identifier: clang lexes it, the port does not (a table of Unicode's names to add to the lexer)"
  :decided "CX2; the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known named-ucn:"]}
 {:id :not-cxx
  :title "not a C++ file (libstdc++'s Makefile.am)"
  :kind :na
  :why "not a C++ file (libstdc++'s Makefile.am, in the headers' corpus): clang's raw lexer reads it differently from the port at an apostrophe"
  :decided "CX2; the kind CX10's; :na by CP260 (a) (the user, 2026-11-08): no reference stream, no verdict to pass"
  :match [#"^known not-cxx:"]}
 {:id :target-option
  :title "an option for a target other than the host's (-march=...): g++ rejects the file"
  :kind :na
  :why "an option for a target other than the host's (-march=...): g++ rejects the file, so it has no reference stream"
  :decided "CX2; the kind CX10's; :na by CP260 (a) (the user, 2026-11-08): no reference stream, no verdict to pass"
  :match [#"^known target-option:"]}
 {:id :raw-udl-suffix
  :title "an identifier touching a literal: libcpp's raw lexing takes it as the literal's suffix, clang's and the port's leave it apart"
  :kind :design
  :why "an identifier touching a string or character literal (\"text\"MACRO): libcpp's raw lexing takes it as the literal's user-defined suffix unless it names a macro (lex.cc's is_macro_not_literal_suffix) and the raw lexing runs no #define, where clang's raw lexer and the port leave a suffix without its underscore apart; at pp libcpp knows the macro and splits as the port does (the stream agrees)"
  :decided "pp-ref (2026-11-20, CP414 (a): the lex level by libcpp's raw lexer, the differences explained): a convention of the raw lexers, the port following clang's"
  :match [#"^known raw-udl-suffix:"]}
 {:id :unterminated-raw-string
  :title "an unterminated raw string at the file's end: libcpp's token ends at its line's end, clang's and the port's at the file's"
  :kind :design
  :why "an unterminated raw string at the file's end (an error test, both reject it): libcpp's raw token ends at its line's end, clang's and the port's at the file's"
  :decided "pp-ref (2026-11-20, CP414 (a)): a convention of the raw lexers on an error test, the port following clang's"
  :match [#"^known unterminated-raw-string:"]}
 {:id :non-xid-utf8
  :title "valid UTF-8 characters no identifier's: libcpp lexes the run as one identifier, clang and the port a token each"
  :kind :design
  :why "valid UTF-8 characters that are no identifier's (C++23's -pedantic-errors test): libcpp lexes the run as one identifier and diagnoses it, clang's raw lexer and the port give each character an unknown token of its own; the stream is judged by the raw tokens (the reference rejects, the port reads: CP261 (a)'s rule), which differ so"
  :decided "pp-ref (2026-11-20, CP414 (a)): a convention of the raw lexers, the port following clang's"
  :match [#"^known non-xid-utf8:"]}
]
